  },
  "method": "Private Android GLES3 Moon Herbarium benchmark. Both encoders share an installed APK and UID per V8 profile. Within each profile, before and reuse start different cold processes in each of two matched rounds (AB/BA). All five snapshots within a run observe the same live isolate, process and EGL context. The terminal frame remains held; no encoder records are cleared.",
  "interventions": "The host schedules the probe four seconds after producing the 210th command packet. The V8 worker samples the held state, sleeps for 150 ms, samples again, calls the normal Javet 6.0.3 V8Runtime.await() once, samples, executes void 0 followed by await(), samples again, calls lowMemoryNotification() with records still held, and takes the final sample. Each sample queries V8 then Android memory. The production frame worker already calls await() after its job.",
  "limits": "The first extra await result is recorded; the second return value is not captured. This is a single fixed stage order and idle workload on one device, with two pairs per profile. These comparisons cannot distinguish snapshot allocations from small process changes, measure individual call duration, predict frame cadence during play, or establish behavior under actual OS memory pressure. V8 low-memory notification is a distinct diagnostic intervention. Android Native Heap summary is private dirty malloc pages.",
  "finding": "In all eight cold runs, the quiet period and additional await each changed V8 used heap and physical heap by zero bytes. The first extra await returned false in every run. The subsequent empty JavaScript evaluation and await increased used heap by 288 bytes with unchanged physical heap in every run. Only the final low-memory notification reduced both gauges in all eight. These results give no memory-reclamation reason to add recurring pumps or empty scripts to this host. They do not demonstrate the latency or suitability of forced collection during play.",
  "provenance": {
    "order": "The pump protocol reused the earlier AB/BA order for the allocator experiment. Only the order was shared.",
    "defaultAwait": "The bundled Javet 6.0.3 V8Runtime.await() bytecode delegates to await(RunTillNoMoreTasks). The boolean is a return value, not a count of work or completed GC.",
